   "what_the_market_was_braced_for": "Heading into the Q1 FY2027 print, the market expected Elastic to deliver roughly $469.7M of revenue and $0.58 non-GAAP EPS for the quarter (in line with the company's own $469-470M / $0.57-0.59 guidance), with FY2027 anchored at ~$1.993B revenue and $3.24 non-GAAP EPS. The option-implied move is unknown, but the stock had drifted down about 2.5% over the five sessions before the release, suggesting a cautious setup. Attention was on whether Elastic would beat its own Q1 guide and, more importantly, raise full-year guidance; the consensus FY27 EPS of $3.24 sat near the midpoint of the company's $3.21-$3.29 range, implying the market expected at most a modest raise.",
